.TH GRIMOIRE 1 "2024-01-01" "Grimoire 1.0.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
grimoire \- A magical programming language for game development

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grimoire
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-i | \-\-interactive ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.RI [ FILE ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Grimoire
is a magical programming language designed for game development with hierarchical autonomous agents, immutable pacts, and emergent AI behaviors. It features a three-tier agent system (Archons, Spirits, Familiars), an immutable pact system for secure contracts, and a comprehensive monitoring system called the Familiar Wrangler.

The language uses thematic terminology to make programming more immersive and intuitive for game developers. Functions are called "rituals", output is "scrying", and variables are "bound" rather than assigned.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.

.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Start the interactive REPL (Read-Eval-Print Loop) mode.

.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug mode with verbose output.

.TP
.I FILE
Grimoire source file to execute (.grim extension recommended).

.SH LANGUAGE FEATURES

.SS Core Syntax
Grimoire uses Python-like indentation and magical terminology:

.RS
.B Variables:
.br
bind x = 42
.br
bind name = "Wizard"

.B Functions (Rituals):
.br
ritual greet(name):
.br
    scry $SCROLL("Hello, " + name + "!")

.B Control Flow:
.br
if condition:
.br
    # code block
.br
elif other_condition:
.br
    # code block
.br
else:
.br
    # code block

.B Loops:
.br
for item in collection:
.br
    # code block
.br
while condition:
.br
    # code block
.RE

.SS Scrying System (Output)
Grimoire provides thematic output variants:

.RS
.B $SCROLL(text)
- Standard text output
.br
.B $CRYSTAL(data)
- Structured data display
.br
.B $FLAME(message)
- Urgent/important messages
.br
.B $MIRROR(reflection)
- Debug/reflection output
.br
.B $RUNE(symbol)
- Symbolic/magical output
.RE

.SS Hierarchical Agent System
The core innovation of Grimoire is its three-tier autonomous agent architecture:

.RS
.B Archons (Strategic Level)
- High-level AI managing multiple spirits
- Domain-specific strategic goals
- Resource allocation across domains
- Domains: Combat, Economy, Diplomacy, Exploration, Defense

.B Spirits (Tactical Level)
- Mid-level AI managing multiple familiars
- Short-term tactical objectives
- Pact creation and management
- Domain authority enforcement

.B Familiars (Operational Level)
- Low-level AI for direct entity management
- Reactive and proactive behaviors
- Activity logging and reporting
- Pact execution and compliance
.RE

.SS Immutable Pact System
Pacts are secure, immutable agreements between spirits and familiars:

.RS
- Immutable after creation
- Black-box security model
- True name authentication
- Spirit-controlled creation and revocation
- Initialization-only binding
.RE

.SS Familiar Wrangler
Centralized monitoring system for all agents:

.RS
- Activity logging and categorization
- Selective reporting by activity type
- Performance statistics
- Cross-agent communication tracking
- Real-time system status
.RE

.SH BUILT-IN FUNCTIONS

.SS Agent Creation
.TP
.B create_archon(name, domain, goals)
Create a strategic-level archon with specified domain and goals.

.TP
.B create_spirit(name, domain, goals)
Create a tactical-level spirit with domain authority.

.TP
.B summon(name, pacts)
Create a familiar with specified pacts.

.TP
.B create_familiar_with_pact(name, pact_terms)
Create a familiar with a single pact binding.

.SS Pact Management
.TP
.B invoke_pact(familiar_name, pact_name)
Invoke a specific pact behavior on a familiar.

.TP
.B revoke_pact(familiar_name, pact_name)
Revoke a pact (destroys the familiar).

.TP
.B get_pact_summary()
Get comprehensive information about all active pacts.

.SS Monitoring & Debugging
.TP
.B enable_reporting(familiar_name, types)
Enable activity reporting for specified types.

.TP
.B disable_reporting(familiar_name)
Disable activity reporting for a familiar.

.TP
.B get_wrangler_report()
Get comprehensive system status from the Familiar Wrangler.

.TP
.B get_familiar_stats(familiar_name)
Get detailed statistics for a specific familiar.

.SS System Management
.TP
.B autonomous_update(agent_name)
Trigger autonomous update cycle for an agent.

.TP
.B oversee_domain(spirit_name, domain)
Check domain authority and resolve conflicts.

.TP
.B true_name(entity)
Get the cryptographic true name of an entity.

.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
The interactive REPL provides extensive debugging and exploration capabilities:

.SS Basic Commands
.TP
.B help()
Show general help information.

.TP
.B help('topic')
Show help for a specific topic.

.TP
.B exit, quit, q
Exit the REPL.

.TP
.B clear
Clear the screen.

.TP
.B version
Show version information.

.SS Debugging Commands
.TP
.B debug on/off
Toggle debug mode.

.TP
.B show_tokens
Show lexer tokens for the next input.

.TP
.B show_ast
Show parser AST for the next input.

.SS Agent Monitoring
.TP
.B agents()
List all active agents.

.TP
.B familiars()
List all active familiars.

.TP
.B wrangler()
Show Familiar Wrangler status.

.SH EXAMPLES

.SS Hello World
.nf
scry $SCROLL("Hello, magical world!")
.fi

.SS Simple Function
.nf
ritual greet(name):
    scry $SCROLL("Greetings, " + name + "!")

greet("Wizard")
.fi

.SS Agent System
.nf
# Create strategic archon
create_archon("BattleCommander", "Combat", ["defend_base"])

# Create tactical spirit
create_spirit("Guardian", "Combat", ["patrol_area"])

# Create operational familiar
create_familiar_with_pact("scout", "patrol_perimeter")

# Enable monitoring
enable_reporting("scout", ["environmental", "command"])

# Check system status
get_wrangler_report()
.fi

.SS RPG System
.nf
bind player_health = 100
bind player_mana = 50

ritual cast_spell(spell_name, cost):
    if player_mana >= cost:
        player_mana = player_mana - cost
        scry $FLAME("✨ Cast " + spell_name + "!")
        return true
    else:
        scry $SCROLL("❌ Not enough mana")
        return false

# Create healing familiar
create_familiar_with_pact("healer", "heal_when_low_health")
cast_spell("Healing Light", 25)
.fi

